    "perplexity": {
      "description": "BASIC is the self-titled album by BASIC, released on No Quarter and drawing from electronic and rock textures. The record’s title suggests a pared-down, elemental approach, and the music lives up to that idea with a sound that emphasizes pulse, atmosphere, and abrasion over ornament.\n\nAs a self-titled release, BASIC functions as a clear statement of identity: it presents the group’s core aesthetic in direct form, balancing machine-like rhythms with guitar-driven weight and textural detail. Issued on No Quarter, a label associated with adventurous indie and experimental work, the album fits comfortably into a lineage of forward-looking recordings that blur genre boundaries while remaining tightly focused in mood and construction.",
